{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Too Many Cooks"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Pinch of Salt"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le07ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be crazy about something"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to like very much"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think she's crazy about coffee."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about beliefs and opinions."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recipe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of instructions for preparing a particular dish, including a list of the ingredients required"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you talk to Amy about helping you with some of the recipes?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go without"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to live with the absence of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She thinks that I'm too addicted to sugar and fat, thus I will not be able to go without them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to forgo"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give something up"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She likes to cook with meat and butter and salt and cheese, all the things I have to forgo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to break"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "interrupt; stop"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have to completely eliminate these unhealthy foods or else we cannot break our addictions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to eliminate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to completely remove or get rid of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's very difficult to eliminate salt from your diet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le07ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Using Linkers to Express Result"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use adverbial expressions to talk about a consequence or result of an action or situation. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I sent them this morning and <span class=\"strong\">consequently</span> you should have received them by now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are many times when you will need to talk about a consequence of an action or situation. In both speaking and writing, there are adverbial expressions that you can use to do this."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I broke my glasses yesterday. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Thus, Consequently, <br /> Therefore, <br /> As a result, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I had to go to the optician and have them replaced. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I broke my glasses yesterday <span class=\\\"underline\\\">and </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Thus, consequently <br /> therefore <br /> as a result </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">had to go to the optician and have them replaced. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">as a result</span> at the end of the sentence. <br />  I broke my glasses yesterday and had to go to the optician and have them replaced <span class=\"strong\"> as a result. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can also talk about what happens when you <span class=\"underline\">don't </span> do something. <br /> We need to protect our natural resources now, <span class=\"strong\"> otherwise </span> there will be nothing left for future generations. <br />We need to protect our natural resources now<span class=\"strong\">  or else </span> there will be nothing left for future generations. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "My wifi wasn't working when I got home, <span class=\"strong\">otherwise</span> I would have sent them last night."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She thinks that I'm too addicted to sugar and fat, <span class=\"strong\">thus</span> I will not be able to go without them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I explained it to her in more detail. <span class=\"strong\">Consequently</span>, she wants to try it too. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Negatives in Reporting"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use your own words to report what someone says. You can also report what someone didn't say by making the reporting verb or the clause itself negative."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The librarian didn't think that the recipes would be hard to follow. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to express what someone did not say, you can use the reporting verb in the negative."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I spoke with my mother for over an hour this morning, but she <span class=\"strong\"> didn't say </span> anything about the dinner party she went to last night. I had to call my aunt to find out what happened at the dinner party. <br />(meaning: \u201cmy mother said nothing about the dinner party\u201d)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If someone says something in the negative, you can simply express this in the reported clause or in the reporting clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Mario</span>: \u201cThis movie isn't exciting and the actors can't act.\u201d <br />Mario <span class=\"strong\">thought</span> the movie <span class=\"strong\">wasn't</span> exciting and the actors <span class=\"strong\">couldn't</span> act. (in the reported clause) <br /> <span class=\"strong\">Lana</span>: \u201cI don't think so because the acting is amazing.\u201d <br /> Lana<span class=\"strong\"> didn't agree </span>because the acting was amazing. (in the reporting clause)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We more commonly report negative sentences with some verbs, however, by changing the reporting verb. These are verbs like: <span class=\"strong\">expect, intend, believe, feel, suppose, think, want, propose, </span> and <span class=\"strong\">plan</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Maya: \u201cI suppose there isn't any more sugar in the pantry.\u201d <br />  Olga <span class=\"strong\">didn't suppose</span> there was any more sugar in the pantry. <br /> Ricardo: \u201cI don't think there is any more flour in the pantry.\u201d <br />  Ricardo <span class=\"strong\">didn't think</span> there was any more flour in the pantry."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She didn't feel like it was a good idea to cut out coffee."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She didn't believe that I was going to do a cleanse."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She didn't expect that she would be able to help with the cooking."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She felt that she wouldn't be a good vegan cook."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find out about your classmates' food addictions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, write at least 5 questions to get information about what foods and ingredients your classmates are addicted to."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your questions to 5 people and record their answers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Summarize your results in a paragraph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Report your findings to your group or class. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write 5 survey questions about food addictions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my questions to 5 people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I record the responses of 5 people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I summarize my findings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my findings to a group."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override